      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1324",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Hypostomus cochliodon Kner, 1854</li><li>Common names: LDA051, Cochliodon Pleco L310, Apricot Pleco, Abrikossugemalle (Denmark)</li><li>Type locality: Rio Cuiabá, Brazil</li><li>Pronunciation: hi POSS tow muss - cock LEE oh don</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1324",
      "html": "<p>South America: Paraguay and middle Paraná River basins (La Plata, Paraná, Middle Paraná; La Plata, Paraná, Paraguay; Bermejo; Upper Paraguay, Cuiabá). IUCN Red List category: Least Concern (last assessed 2020).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1324",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.3 - 7.2</li><li>Temperature: 21 - 24°C</li><li>Hardness: dH 10 - 18</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1324",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1324",
      "html": "<p>Very similar to L137 from the Rio Tapajós and similar to L310 from Bahia, both in Brazil. Previously placed in Cochliodon and now included in the larger genus Hypostomus as a member of the Hypostomus cochliodon group. All these species have higher backs than other conspecifics and spoon-shaped teeth (like Panaque).</p><p>Etymology: Greek hypo = under + Greek stoma = mouth. From the Latin coclea (coch-), for spoon, and the Greek odon, for tooth, in reference to the fact that the teeth are about half as spoon-shaped as those of wood-specializing members of the Hypostomus cochliodon group.</p>"
    },
    {
